Yes. Run these commands inside Google Cloud SDK Shell.

cd /d D:\AI_Personal_Buddy\Node_Backend

Then:

gcloud config set project python-microservice-hub
gcloud auth login
gcloud auth configure-docker asia-south1-docker.pkg.dev

Press Y when asked.

Then test the push:

docker push asia-south1-docker.pkg.dev/python-microservice-hub/buddy-backend-repo/buddy-node-backend:latest

After the push succeeds, run:

deploy.bat

So your regular deployment process in Google Cloud SDK Shell is simply:

cd /d D:\AI_Personal_Buddy\Node_Backend
deploy.bat

You only need to run the login and Docker configuration commands again if authentication expires or you change accounts.